<Admonition type="note" title="">

* The **document expiration** feature deletes a document once the time you schedule for it has passed.  
  Use *document expiration* for documents that are needed only for a limited time, like documents that hold shopping
  carts, login sessions, or cached data.  
  Deleting the document triggers features that react to the deletion of documents, like indexing, replication, and ETL tasks.

* To schedule a document's expiration, set the `@expires` [metadata](../../../client-api/session/how-to/get-and-modify-entity-metadata.mdx)
  property of the document to the intended expiration time.

* To enable *document expiration* for a database, send the server an `ExpirationConfiguration` object using the
  [ConfigureExpirationOperation](../../../documents/document-expiration/client-api.mdx#configureexpirationoperation) operation.  
  The `ExpirationConfiguration` object also sets the frequency at which the *document expiration* feature checks the database
  for documents whose expiration time has passed.

* To enable and configure *document expiration* using Studio, see
  [Document Expiration: Studio View](../../../documents/document-expiration/document-expiration-view.mdx).

